      "question": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are different complex numbers with $|\\beta|=1$, then $|\\frac{\\beta-\\alpha}{1-\\bar{\\alpha}\\beta}|$ is equal to",
      "options": [
        "0",
        "1",
        "2",
        "1/2"
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "(b) 1",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$|\\frac{\\beta-\\alpha}{1-\\bar{\\alpha}\\beta}|^2 = (\\frac{\\beta-\\alpha}{1-\\bar{\\alpha}\\beta})(\\frac{\\bar{\\beta}-\\bar{\\alpha}}{1-\\alpha\\bar{\\beta}})$.",
        "Since $\\beta\\bar{\\beta} = |\\beta|^2 = 1$, we have $\\bar{\\beta} = 1/\\beta$.",
        "Substitute and simplify to get 1."
      ]
